## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkZZZMawAAgC4f?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/khemaridh/article/2065211366953369879/media/2065209828176478208) I built a "headless CRM" in Codex [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1993486891098759168/gtfYOnT3_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/khemaridh) [Khe Hy](http://x.com/khemaridh) [@khemaridh](http://x.com/khemaridh) · 11h Follow...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Khe Hy</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/khemaridh">@khemaridh</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2065191795487821824">http://x.com/i/article/2065191795487821824</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2065191795487821824">http://x.com/i/article/2065191795487821824</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkZZZMawAAgC4f?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/khemaridh/article/2065211366953369879/media/2065209828176478208)<br/>I built a "headless CRM" in Codex<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1993486891098759168/gtfYOnT3_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/khemaridh)<br/>[Khe Hy](http://x.com/khemaridh)<br/>[@khemaridh](http://x.com/khemaridh)<br/>·<br/>11h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow khemaridh<br/>3<br/>1<br/>22<br/>[7.6K](http://x.com/khemaridh/status/2065211366953369879/analytics)<br/>How to connect Gmail and iMessage to build better relationships<br/>I miss my OpenClaw.<br/>I retired “Agent Twilo” in March when Anthropic banned 3rd party access to the Claude Max plan.<br/>And since then I’ve been looking for alternatives — particularly options with easy access from an iPhone.<br/>This week, I started building a Codex-driven solution that works well inside the ChatGPT app. It was inspired by fintech entrepreneur <br/>[@nicolas](https://x.com/@nicolas)<br/>’ post <br/>[My agent stack for automating my personal life.](https://x.com/nicbstme/status/2060583553449250888)<br/>## <br/>Building my customized personal agent<br/>I’m on my phone all the time.<br/>Texting, emailing, sending screenshots and calling friends.<br/>I share YouTube tutorials, make <br/>[mutually beneficial introductions](https://radreads.co/mututally-beneficial-intro/)<br/> and send birthday videos.<br/>Basically, I use my phone to try to be helpful to others (and get them excited about the possibilities of AI).<br/>I have no interest in replacing this sincere approach with an AI-enabled system.<br/>Yet at the same time, I do want to use AI to give me more moments of serendipity and suggest more ways to help others.<br/>So the goal was simple.<br/>How can I surface interesting insights in my work email (for <br/>[Latourai.com](https://www.latourai.com/)<br/>) and inside my iMessages?<br/>Why these two services? Because that’s where 90% of my communications take place. And iMessage has become a much bigger source of my overall communications.<br/>So I set out to build this using OpenAI’s Codex.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkZlXKaIAAy9hv?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/khemaridh/article/2065211366953369879/media/2065210033789607936)<br/>## <br/>What is a headless CRM?<br/>Headless software is all the rage these days.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkZqUSaYAA-0Lz?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/khemaridh/article/2065211366953369879/media/2065210118917218304)<br/>We’ve got headless CRMs, browsers and business intelligence tools. But what does this term actually mean?<br/>It means there’s no user interface. With headless software, you can’t click and use your mouse. Interactions happen exclusively via text (chat, scripts, APIs and agents).<br/>What does that mean in CRM terms? It means that you can use natural language to interact with your underlying contacts. For example, you could say:<br/>* Tell me which clients have signed a purchase agreement but haven’t closed<br/>* I’m going to a conference in Dallas, which high-quality leads should I pursue while I’m there?<br/>These don’t require an interface. It just requires safely connecting my data to the Codex harness.<br/>## <br/>Step 1: Selecting a harness<br/>The first order of business was where this “app” would be hosted and how I would communicate with it.<br/>Some common “harnesses” are Claude Cowork, Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw, Hermes and Pi.<br/>I chose Codex because its mobile experience has gotten really good. It can reference all your chats and any required files (and is blazingly fast).<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkZtkBasAAr3u3?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/khemaridh/article/2065211366953369879/media/2065210174680510464)<br/>## <br/>Step 2: Connecting iMessage and Google<br/>This was the trickiest step since it involved using two open source “CLIs” to connect to each service.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkZvaLbAAAnHjQ?format=jpg&amp;name=sma</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 42 · 🔁 1 · 💬 3 · 🔖 116</p><p><a href="https://x.com/khemaridh/status/2065211366953369879">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
