## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKdSg2OXwAAy_ow?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/zackpaid/article/2064739027484287329/media/2064709678437744640) how to find winning meta ads angles with claude fable 5.0 [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2055480268564123649/5ijM3Y6V_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/zackpaid) [zack](http://x.com/zackpaid)...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>zack</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/zackpaid">@zackpaid</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064697289105383424">http://x.com/i/article/2064697289105383424</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064697289105383424">http://x.com/i/article/2064697289105383424</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKdSg2OXwAAy_ow?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/zackpaid/article/2064739027484287329/media/2064709678437744640)<br/>how to find winning meta ads angles with claude fable 5.0 <br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2055480268564123649/5ijM3Y6V_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/zackpaid)<br/>[zack](http://x.com/zackpaid)<br/>[@zackpaid](http://x.com/zackpaid)<br/>·<br/>Jun 10<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow zackpaid<br/>1<br/>7<br/>64<br/>[6.1K](http://x.com/zackpaid/status/2064739027484287329/analytics)<br/>for years the meta ads library research process looked like this:<br/>open a browser. manually search competitor after competitor. screenshot interesting ads into a messy google doc. try to remember what you were looking for. spend 45 minutes to get 10 minutes of useful intelligence. build your angle strategy from half-remembered observations and gut feel.<br/>that workflow is over.<br/>claude fable 5 is anthropic's new state-of-the-art vision model. and "vision" here goes way past looking at one image and describing it. fable 5 does autonomous visual navigation at a level no previous model could match. it can scroll, browse, screenshot, extract, and analyze at a depth that makes manual research feel like reading by candlelight.<br/>here's exactly how we're using it to find winning ad angles faster than any human researcher could.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKdtJG2W0AEQSf8?format=png&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/zackpaid/article/2064739027484287329/media/2064738957397512193)<br/>## <br/>what fable 5's vision capabilities actually mean<br/>the announcement said fable 5 is "state-of-the-art for tasks involving vision" and can "rebuild a web app's source code from screenshots alone."<br/>that second sentence is the one that matters for advertisers.<br/>it means fable 5 reads the architecture behind a landing page or ad creative, not just the surface of it. the structural decisions. the copywriting framework. the psychological triggers embedded in the layout. the conversion mechanics.<br/>previous models needed complex harnesses and scaffolding to navigate visual environments. fable 5 does it with a minimal, vision-only setup.<br/>for competitive research, this means you can now have an autonomous research agent that:<br/>* browses the meta ads library on your behalf<br/>* identifies and categorizes every competitor angle it finds<br/>* analyzes which creatives have been running longest (the surest proxy for what's working)<br/>* extracts specific copy patterns, hook structures, and visual approaches<br/>* cross-references findings against your own account's historical performance<br/>all without you touching a browser.<br/>## <br/>workflow 1: autonomous competitive research with claude cowork<br/>claude cowork is the desktop tool that lets claude operate your computer directly, clicking, scrolling, and extracting information from any application or website.<br/>paired with fable 5's vision capabilities, it becomes an autonomous research analyst.<br/>the setup:<br/>open claude cowork. assign fable 5 as the model. give it this instruction:<br/>"go to the meta ads library at <br/>[facebook.com/ads/library](http://facebook.com/ads/library)<br/>. search for \[COMPETITOR NAMES AND CATEGORY\]. for every ad that has been running for more than 3 months, extract: the ad angle, the hook structure, the visual format, the estimated audience, and the landing page destination. organize findings by angle type and flag the top 5 creatives by estimated longevity. compile into a structured competitive intelligence report."<br/>fable 5 navigates the library, scrolls through results, identifies run dates, clicks through to landing pages, reads copy, and produces a structured report.<br/>what used to take 45 minutes of tedious manual work takes 8 minutes of autonomous research.<br/>## <br/>workflow 2: scrolling facebook and instagram feeds for native angle discovery<br/>the meta ads library shows declared ads. the f</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 71 · 🔁 9 · 💬 1 · 🔖 201</p><p><a href="https://x.com/zackpaid/status/2064739027484287329">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
