## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKel0x8W4AAXzI_?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/seelffff/article/2064831856164430010/media/2064801280350937088) Claude - My Personal Ghostwriter [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1997602591966953472/ilSxeidg_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/seelffff) [self.dll](http://x.com/seelffff) [@seelffff](http://x.com/seelffff) · 18h · Follow...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>self.dll</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/seelffff">@seelffff</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064783698889756672">http://x.com/i/article/2064783698889756672</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064783698889756672">http://x.com/i/article/2064783698889756672</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKel0x8W4AAXzI_?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/seelffff/article/2064831856164430010/media/2064801280350937088)<br/>Claude - My Personal Ghostwriter<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1997602591966953472/ilSxeidg_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/seelffff)<br/>[self.dll](http://x.com/seelffff)<br/>[@seelffff](http://x.com/seelffff)<br/>·<br/>18h<br/>·<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow seelffff<br/>3<br/>5<br/>45<br/>[3K](http://x.com/seelffff/status/2064831856164430010/analytics)<br/># <br/>The $1,718 per 2 weeks<br/>Last 2 weeks X paid me $1,718 in revenue sharing. Not for selling a course. Not for ads. For doing the thing I'd already be doing anyway - digging through AI tools all day and posting what I find.<br/>Here's the part nobody sees: the routine behind this account isn't done by me anymore. It’s handled by an agent I use on a daily basis. It reads the feed, scores topics, learns from my analytics and writes drafts in my voice. I just pick, tweak and hit publish.<br/>This article is the exact system. Not theory - the actual files, the actual code, the actual numbers.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKe8lAGW4AAmVos?format=png&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/seelffff/article/2064831856164430010/media/2064826298040508416)<br/># <br/>How It Works<br/>One run, four stages. No frameworks, no orchestration - a script, a model, and three markdown files.<br/>1. Collect. The script pulls GitHub trending, the Hacker News front page, and my inbox file - a note where I dump anything that caught my eye during the day: links, questions from my replies, half-formed ideas.<br/>2. Score. The model gets all of it together with my style, my memory and my analytics - and ranks the 5 best topics. Each topic gets a score out of 10, a format, and one line on why my audience would care.<br/>3. Draft. For the top 2 topics it writes complete posts in my voice, in both languages, plus an idea for the visual - what to record or screenshot.<br/>4. Review. I read, kill what's weak, tweak what's good, publish. The agent never posts anything itself. That's not a technical limitation - that's the design.<br/>![](https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2064824561019850752/img/PvlI1wA2qkSycaiO.jpg)<br/>After every run the agent saves a note like this into topics/ - a real example, trimmed to three topics:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKeicfMWYAASvbZ?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/seelffff/article/2064831856164430010/media/2064797564465995776)<br/>How to read it: topic - score out of 10 - which of my 7 formats fits. The line below is the argument - why my audience specifically would care. The score comes from four factors: how fresh the topic is, whether there are concrete numbers to hook with, how it matches my audience's interests from analytics, and whether big accounts have already covered it. That's exactly why topic #3 got a 6/10 - solid story, but the window had closed.<br/># <br/>The Folder<br/>Everything lives in one folder inside my Obsidian vault. Plain markdown plus one Python script. If I delete the script tomorrow, the brain survives - it's all in the files.<br/>plaintext<br/>```plaintext<br/>agent/<br/>├── style.md      - how I write (the agent's taste)<br/>├── memory.md     - what's been posted, what's rejected<br/>├── analytics.md  - what actually works, from real numbers<br/>├── replies.md    - how I comment on other people's posts<br/>├── agent.py      - the agent itself (~100 lines)<br/>├── topics/<br/>│   ├── inbox.md  - raw material I collect during the day<br/>│   └── scored topics land here after every run<br/>└── drafts/<br/>    └── ready-to-post drafts land here<br/>```<br/># <br/>Brain #1: style.md - the Agent's Taste<br/>The agent doesn't “write like an AI” because it's not allowed to. I exported 182 of my posts, had the model extract the patterns, then added my own bans on top. The result is a contract the agent can't break:<br/>* everything lowercase, no hashtags, emojis only in memes<br/>* first line is</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 61 · 🔁 6 · 💬 4 · 🔖 105</p><p><a href="https://x.com/seelffff/status/2064831856164430010">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
