## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKd8KnlaEAA6SSp?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/itsalexvacca/article/2064755591764230491/media/2064755476039077888) Build Your GTM AI in This Exact Order: The 7-Layer Stack Behind Our $7M System [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909705035052990467/pnfX3LA__normal.jpg)](http://x.com/itsalexvacca) [Alex...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Alex Vacca</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/itsalexvacca">@itsalexvacca</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2061785866385911808">http://x.com/i/article/2061785866385911808</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2061785866385911808">http://x.com/i/article/2061785866385911808</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKd8KnlaEAA6SSp?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/itsalexvacca/article/2064755591764230491/media/2064755476039077888)<br/>Build Your GTM AI in This Exact Order: The 7-Layer Stack Behind Our $7M System<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1909705035052990467/pnfX3LA__normal.jpg)](http://x.com/itsalexvacca)<br/>[Alex Vacca](http://x.com/itsalexvacca)<br/>[@itsalexvacca](http://x.com/itsalexvacca)<br/>·<br/>8h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow itsalexvacca<br/>1<br/>3<br/>29<br/>[2.3K](http://x.com/itsalexvacca/status/2064755591764230491/analytics)<br/>Most explanations of agentic AI are written to sound impressive, not to be understood. They stack jargon on jargon until the person who actually has to make a decision walks away more confused than when they started.<br/>So here's the version I use with our team and with the 400+ B2B companies we've built GTM systems for at ColdIQ. Seven layers. Each one is a building block, and each one adds something the layer beneath it can't do on its own.<br/>The useful part isn't the diagram. It's knowing which layer you're actually operating on, because most companies think they're running agents when they're really running a chatbot with extra steps.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJzv1NNasAElmXU?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/itsalexvacca/article/2064755591764230491/media/2061786426786885633)<br/>The 7 layers of agentic AI, each building on the one below it<br/>I'll define each layer in plain language, then show you exactly where it lives inside the system we run every day. Including the one place we tried to climb higher and chose to come back down.<br/># <br/>Layer 1: Machine Learning (the foundation)<br/>This is the floor. It's AI learning patterns from data instead of following rules a human hand-coded.<br/>Three flavors live here. <br/>Supervised learning trains on labeled examples, the way you'd teach with flashcards. Unsupervised learning finds patterns nobody pointed it at. Reinforcement learning optimizes through trial and error, getting better each time it's rewarded for a good outcome.<br/>You're already touching this layer every day, often without noticing. Lead scoring models, send-time optimization, deliverability prediction. None of it talks. All of it learns.<br/>Layer 1 in practice: the scoring that happens before a single email<br/>We ran a campaign recently where the total addressable market was 15,000 companies. Before anything went out, every account passed through a weighted scoring model built on our own closed-won data. Funding stage, firmographics through Clay and FullEnrich, technographics through BuiltWith, growth signals through PredictLeads and Crunchbase.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJzwlTzawAA3seb?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/itsalexvacca/article/2064755591764230491/media/2061787253190606848)<br/>Layer 1 in practice: AI scoring cut a 15,000-company TAM to 8,900 before any email went out<br/>It cut the list to 8,900\. More than 40% gone, not because they were bad companies, but because the timing or the fit was wrong. Some had just raised and frozen spend, some showed zero hiring activity, some had adopted a competitor the month before.<br/>That's Layer 1 earning its keep. <br/>Signal-based targeting like this produces 2 to 4x the performance of unscored outreach, in every campaign we run, with no exceptions I've seen across 400+ clients. The list is the strategy, and the list gets decided by a model before a human writes a word. I broke the full four-dimension scoring model down <br/>[in this post](https://x.com/itsalexvacca/status/2041547607995228198)<br/> if you want the mechanics.<br/># <br/>Layer 2: Large Language Models (the processor)<br/>Now the machine understands and produces language.<br/>An LLM processes enormous amounts of text, holds context across a long conversation, and increasingly handles images and audio alongside words. This is the layer that mad</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 49 · 🔁 4 · 💬 1 · 🔖 95</p><p><a href="https://x.com/itsalexvacca/status/2064755591764230491">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
