## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKZdjSlXwAAymKr?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/Mnilax/article/2064447011953225770/media/2064440340061339648) Claude Fable 5: the exact setup to get maximum quality before the free window closes [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2007608177492217856/3gdItGwC_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/Mnilax) [Mnimiy](http://x.com/Mnilax)...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Mnimiy</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/Mnilax">@Mnilax</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064425685834207232">http://x.com/i/article/2064425685834207232</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064425685834207232">http://x.com/i/article/2064425685834207232</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKZdjSlXwAAymKr?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/Mnilax/article/2064447011953225770/media/2064440340061339648)<br/>Claude Fable 5: the exact setup to get maximum quality before the free window closes<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2007608177492217856/3gdItGwC_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/Mnilax)<br/>[Mnimiy](http://x.com/Mnilax)<br/>[@Mnilax](http://x.com/Mnilax)<br/>·<br/>17h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow Mnilax<br/>7<br/>25<br/>274<br/>[38K](http://x.com/Mnilax/status/2064447011953225770/analytics)<br/>On roughly 1 in 20 prompts, the most capable Claude model ever shipped won't be the one answering you.<br/>Most people will flip the dropdown to Fable 5 today and never notice the three flagged areas where it quietly hands the prompt to a weaker model, or that the free access closes in 13 days.<br/>I spent launch day putting it on four real projects and mapping every fallback trigger and config knob, so you don't burn the window guessing.<br/>Below: the exact setup to pull maximum Fable 5 quality before the meter turns on, where it silently routes you to Opus 4.8, and the bugs it surfaced that nothing caught for months.<br/># <br/>What actually shipped<br/>Two models, one brain.<br/>Fable 5 is the new flagship, available to everyone. Mythos 5 is the same underlying model with the cybersecurity safeguards lifted, restricted to Project Glasswing partners and a coming trusted-access program. The only thing separating the two is the safeguards.<br/>The name is the tell: fable comes from the Latin fabula, "that which is told," a sibling in meaning to the Greek mythos. It is the strongest model Anthropic has ever put in front of the public.<br/>On SWE-Bench Pro it scores 80.3% against Opus 4.8's 69.2%, GPT 5.5's 58.6%, and Gemini 3.1 Pro's 54.2%. On Terminal-Bench 2.1, 88.0%. On GDPval-AA knowledge work, 1932 to Opus 4.8's 1890.<br/>The pattern that matters more than any single number: the longer and more complex the task, the bigger the lead. This is not a model that wins on one-liners. It wins on the jobs you've been afraid to hand off.<br/>Price is $10 per million input tokens, $50 per million output. Less than half of what Mythos Preview cost.<br/>The advantage compounds on big work. In early testing, Stripe ran a codebase-wide migration on a 50-million-line Ruby codebase in a single day, work that would have taken a team over two months by hand.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKZfV3eWwAAw8-Y?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/Mnilax/article/2064447011953225770/media/2064442308469112832)<br/># <br/>The silent fallback: \~5% of the time you're not talking to Fable<br/>This is the part nobody is going to read in the announcement, and it changes how you route work.<br/>Fable ships with a set of classifiers: separate systems that watch each prompt. When a request looks like it touches cybersecurity, biology and chemistry, or distillation, the response is handled by Claude Opus 4.8 instead of Fable, and you get told it happened.<br/>More than 95% of sessions never hit a fallback. For those sessions, Fable 5 is effectively identical to Mythos 5\. The premium model is the default experience.<br/>But if your work lives in one of those three buckets, you are often getting Opus 4.8, not the flagship you selected. Three things to internalize:<br/>* Security work falls back, by design. The cyber classifier is built to stop Fable from making progress on offensive tasks. Under automated red-teaming, Fable's offensive-task success rate sits at 5.4%, down from Opus 4.8's 56.6% and Opus 4.6's 83.2%. That's not Fable being worse at security. That's the safeguard doing exactly its job. If you do pentest, exploit, or red-team work, expect the fallback and don't waste turns fighting it.<br/>* Bio and chem are netted broadly right now. Anthropic tuned these conservatively to ship safely and fast, which means even benign chemistry or biology questions can trigger a fa</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 323 · 🔁 26 · 💬 6 · 🔖 619</p><p><a href="https://x.com/Mnilax/status/2064447011953225770">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
