- GitHub - alibaba/open-code-review: Open-source &amp; free — Battle-tested at Alibaba's scale. Hybrid architecture code review tool: deterministic pipelines + LLM Agent, precise line-level comments, built-in fine-tuned ruleset (NPE, thread-safety, XSS, SQL injection), OpenAI &amp; Anthropic compatible. · GitHub: https://github.com/alibaba/open-code-review
- https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKdf9cGWwAAFZfl.jpg: https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKdf9cGWwAAFZfl.jpg</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>AlphaSignal AI</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/AlphaSignalAI">@AlphaSignalAI</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064290620416589824">http://x.com/i/article/2064290620416589824</a></p></blockquote><div><img src="https://opengraph.githubassets.com/7ee3f94016ddb68bd215187b1b2bb7d622e693cccb90288f699705f939c8dbe5/alibaba/open-code-review" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://github.com/alibaba/open-code-review/raw/main/imgs/logo.svg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/e4b8794715fd95b551a5f9151bb4cafdc660ff143c3375aadbae3698a50ed82e/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6e706d2f762f40616c69626162612d67726f75702f6f70656e2d636f64652d7265766965773f7374796c653d666c61742d737175617265" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/aaac266761424237a7f8ac6c51a51a453169fc8881d26a2ca027259d3bed5bea/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6769746875622f616374696f6e732f776f726b666c6f772f7374617475732f616c69626162612f6f70656e2d636f64652d7265766965772f72656c656173652e796d6c3f7374796c653d666c61742d737175617265" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/6fca799dde1e7e5c3d710bbee2cb7ca77f6347a51e0758b933db21a8c7eebd38/68747470733a2f2f676f7265706f7274636172642e636f6d2f62616467652f6769746875622e636f6d2f616c69626162612f6f70656e2d636f64652d7265766965773f7374796c653d666c61742d737175617265" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/81a302e376f278236fe580b923ee7e69db270e5ed4b65b78c325efbb9158be05/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6769746875622f6c6963656e73652f616c69626162612f6f70656e2d636f64652d7265766965773f7374796c653d666c61742d737175617265" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://github.com/alibaba/open-code-review/raw/main/imgs/highlights-en.png" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/43321b7a2f6a055e70a296276197f1c46fc2f3ab0a578258cf51f38645599371/68747470733a2f2f6170692e737461722d686973746f72792e636f6d2f7376673f7265706f733d616c69626162612f6f70656e2d636f64652d72657669657726747970653d44617465" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/></div><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064290620416589824">http://x.com/i/article/2064290620416589824</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKYLkj3bwAAOsvb?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/AlphaSignalAI/article/2064350250786341326/media/2064350201926893568)<br/>The Best AI Code Review Tools Don't Let the Model Do Everything<br/>[![Square profile picture](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2014100845189529600/Ff1Xc28-_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>[AlphaSignal AI](http://x.com/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>[@AlphaSignalAI](http://x.com/AlphaSignalAI)<br/>·<br/>4h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow AlphaSignalAI<br/>1<br/>3<br/>[590](http://x.com/AlphaSignalAI/status/2064350250786341326/analytics)<br/>## <br/>Stop asking the LLM for guarantees. It can only give you judgment.<br/>&gt; In 4 minutes, you'll learn why AI code review fails when models own both reasoning and control, and how Alibaba separates deterministic guarantees from judgment.<br/>Most teams adding AI to their code review workflow do the same thing.<br/>They give a general-purpose agent the diff, write a prompt that says "review this carefully," and hope the output is useful.<br/>Sometimes it is. Often it isn't.<br/>The mistake isn't using an LLM for code review.<br/>The mistake is asking the LLM to provide both judgment and guarantees.<br/>Judgment is probabilistic. Guarantees are deterministic. Open Code Review separates the two.<br/>## <br/>The three things code review requires<br/>Before getting to the architecture, it's worth being precise about what reliable code review actually needs.<br/>Complete coverage. Every file in the changeset gets reviewed. Not most files. Not the files the model decided were important. Every file.<br/>Precise positioning. A reported issue maps to the exact line it describes. Line 247 means line 247, not approximately that area of the file.<br/>Consistent rule enforcement. The same rule applied to the same pattern produces the same result across every file, every run.<br/>These are deterministic requirements. They don't benefit from reasoning. They require guarantees.<br/>A purely language-driven agent can approximate all three. It cannot guarantee any of them. That distinction is where pure LLM code review breaks.<br/>## <br/>What breaks in production<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKYKePxbYAAhUBJ?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/AlphaSignalAI/article/2064350250786341326/media/2064348993942151168)<br/>Open Code Review originated as Alibaba's internal official code review assistant, serving tens of thousands of developers over two years and identifying millions of code defects before being open-sourced.<br/>The README is unusually direct about what failed before the hybrid architecture was built.<br/>Three failure modes appeared consistently when using general-purpose agents.<br/>Incomplete coverage.<br/>On larger changesets, agents cut corners. They selectively review some files and skip others without signaling that anything was skipped. The diff had 40 files. The agent reviewed 12\. You find out when something ships broken.<br/>Position drift.<br/>Reported issues don't match actual code locations. Line numbers drift. File references shift. The agent found a real bug but pointed at the wrong line, so the reviewer can't locate it and the comment gets dismissed.<br/>Unstable quality.<br/>Minor prompt variations cause wild swings in review quality. The same diff reviewed twice with slightly different wording produces completely different feedback. There's no deterministic layer to inspect when something goes wrong.<br/>The root cause is precise: a purely language-driven architecture lacks hard constraints on the review process.<br/>## <br/>The architecture in one sentence<br/>Deterministic engineering owns the decisions that must not go wrong. The LLM owns the decisions that require judgment.<br/>That single boundary is the design.<br/>## <br/>How the boundary works in practice<br/>What deterministic engineering handles:<br/>Precise file selection.<br/>Engineering logic determines exactly which files need review and which should be filtered. N</blockquote><p>🔗 <a href="https://github.com/alibaba/open-code-review">GitHub - alibaba/open-code-review: Open-source &amp; free — Battle-tested at Alibaba's scale. Hybrid architecture code review tool: deterministic pipelines + LLM Agent, precise line-level comments, built-in fine-tuned ruleset (NPE, thread-safety, XSS, SQL injection), OpenAI &amp; Anthropic compatible. · GitHub</a></p><p>🔗 <a href="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKdf9cGWwAAFZfl.jpg">https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKdf9cGWwAAFZfl.jpg</a></p><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 18 · 🔁 1 · 💬 1 · 🔖 31</p><p><a href="https://x.com/AlphaSignalAI/status/2064350250786341326">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
