## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKYRF6AXIAEjUF8?format=png&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/mfpiccolo/article/2064358779940995141/media/2064356272363741185) How to make your Agentic Backend Architecture Production Ready? [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2000231368198852610/YnKhL5h5_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/mfpiccolo) [Mike Piccolo](http://x.com/mfpiccolo)...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Mike Piccolo</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/mfpiccolo">@mfpiccolo</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064355389676650496">http://x.com/i/article/2064355389676650496</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064355389676650496">http://x.com/i/article/2064355389676650496</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKYRF6AXIAEjUF8?format=png&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/mfpiccolo/article/2064358779940995141/media/2064356272363741185)<br/>How to make your Agentic Backend Architecture Production Ready?<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2000231368198852610/YnKhL5h5_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/mfpiccolo)<br/>[Mike Piccolo](http://x.com/mfpiccolo)<br/>[@mfpiccolo](http://x.com/mfpiccolo)<br/>·<br/>20h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow mfpiccolo<br/>4<br/>31<br/>214<br/>[41K](http://x.com/mfpiccolo/status/2064358779940995141/analytics)<br/>Building an agentic backend on iii means composing a handful of workers on the engine. Each one is production-ready. Each one is replaceable. The composition is your backend.<br/>If you see below in the image, harness sequences the agent turn loop. context-manager turns raw history into model-ready context. session-manager is a durable, reactive, branching store of typed conversation entries. llm-router is one front door over every LLM provider.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKYRZQfW0AMxAnC?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/mfpiccolo/article/2064358779940995141/media/2064356604816838659)<br/>Each one is standalone. Install just llm-router and you have provider-agnostic completions for any app. Install just session-manager and you have a reactive conversation store. The harness only sequences the other three plus tool(i.e. function calls) dispatch. Anything that grows real logic, approval gating, spend budgets, multi-agent handoff, becomes its own sibling worker rather than complicating the harness.<br/>From outside this looks like four layers. Inside there is no integration code between them. The harness calls the context-manager with iii.trigger("context::sync"). The context-manager returns. The harness calls the llm-router. The llm-router streams over a channel. No orchestration framework to configure. No contract between layers to maintain. No service mesh to operate.<br/>These four workers run on the same engine as queue worker, state worker, pubsub worker, observability worker, HTTP worker, sandbox worker, schedule/cron worker. Every worker inherits the rest, with zero integration cost. \`iii worker add &lt;worker-name&gt;\`, get the whole system surface. Adding queue support to your llm-router is calling iii.trigger("queue::enqueue"). Adding scheduled retries is calling iii.trigger("cron::schedule"). Adding observability is automatic. These are not separate integrations. They are functions on workers already running.<br/>This is the <br/>[@iiidevs](https://x.com/@iiidevs)<br/> pattern. We noticed complexity in backend engineering eventually demands abstraction, the same way <br/>[@reactjs](https://x.com/@reactjs)<br/> noticed it in UIs. React reduced UIs to Components. iii reduces backends to Worker, Trigger, Function.<br/>The paradigm of "add another service and integrate it into all others" needs to end. Any capability you would have added as a service can be a worker on iii. The functionality is exposed as functions and triggers. What you get is a system that is composable, extensible, discoverable, and observable. One that gets more capable every time anyone adds a worker.<br/>Join us in building the Agentic Backend that the modern world needs:<br/>[ discord.gg/iiidev](http://discord.gg/iiidev)<br/>iii is open source. Get started at<br/>[ iii.dev/docs](https://iii.dev/docs)<br/>. The harness workers are at<br/>[ github.com/iii-hq/workers](https://github.com/iii-hq/workers)<br/> and the engine is at<br/>[ github.com/iii-hq/iii](https://github.com/iii-hq/iii)<br/>.<br/>* [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2000231368198852610/YnKhL5h5_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/mfpiccolo)  <br/>[Mike Piccolo](http://x.com/mfpiccolo)  <br/>[@mfpiccolo](http://x.com/mfpiccolo)  <br/>Follow  <br/>Click to Follow mfpiccolo  <br/>Founder of  <br/>[@iiidevs](http://x.com/iiidevs)  <br/> Co-founder and board member of [http://FullStack.com](https://t.co/imPpSoV4Gu)</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 253 · 🔁 32 · 💬 3 · 🔖 511</p><p><a href="https://x.com/mfpiccolo/status/2064358779940995141">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
